# Paths under the repo root that must NOT be uploaded as public static assets.
#
# `[assets] directory = "."` in wrangler.toml points at the repo root (the same tree GitHub Pages
# serves today), so EVERYTHING here is a publish candidate — including the repo's own plumbing.
# Anything not listed below is served at https://integrauth.com/<path>.
#
# `.git` is the important one: without it, `.git/config`, `.git/HEAD`, the refs and
# `.git/objects/pack/*.pack` all upload, which is the entire repository history downloadable from
# the live site. GitHub Actions checkouts create `.git` too, so CI deploys would publish it as well.
# Verify after changing this file with:
#   WRANGLER_LOG=debug npx wrangler deploy --dry-run 2>&1 | grep 'Ignoring asset'
# (`.assetsignore`, `_headers` and `_redirects` are excluded by wrangler automatically.)
#
# NOT listed here on purpose: `.well-known` (security.txt must stay publicly reachable).
# `.nojekyll` and `CNAME` were GitHub-Pages-only files and were deleted outright at the 2026-08
# cutover (Pages is retired) rather than added here — nothing needs either of them anymore.

# --- repo plumbing (never publish) ---
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.github
.wrangler

# --- local secrets (never publish) ---
# `.dev.vars` is wrangler's standard file for local-dev secrets — it is where IA_WEBSITE_OIDC_SECRET
# and friends live while running `npm run worker:dev`. It is gitignored, but that protects the repo,
# not the deploy: `wrangler deploy` uploads the working tree, so a developer deploying from their own
# machine would publish their live client secret at https://integrauth.com/.dev.vars. Same reasoning
# for `.env`. Both are listed here so the leak is impossible rather than merely unlikely.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*

# --- build/dev tooling, not part of the site ---
node_modules
src
tsconfig.json
package*.json
wrangler.toml

# --- internal working documents: CLAUDE.md, README.md, QUICK_START.md and docs/*.md are notes,
#     not site content, and nothing on the site links to them ---
*.md
docs

# --- gitignored working dirs (never publish) ---
# These are all in .gitignore, so a CI checkout never contains them — but `.assetsignore`'s job is
# to protect the DEPLOY, not the repo: `wrangler deploy` uploads the working tree, so a developer
# deploying from their own machine would otherwise publish local build output, notes and test
# artifacts at https://integrauth.com/<path>. Same reasoning as the `.dev.vars`/`.env` block above.
# Kept in step with .gitignore's own "never deploy to public site" entries.
dist
build
logs
coverage
.nyc_output
.cache
.tmp
.temp
product-plans
dev-notes
